---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Wordmark from '../components/Wordmark.astro';

const beliefs = [
  {
    n: '01',
    title: 'Question the ordinary.',
    lines: [
      'We’ve grown accustomed to countless small inconveniences.',
      'The extra step. The awkward interaction. The workaround we no longer question.',
      'But familiarity doesn’t make something right.',
      'Great ideas often begin with a simple question:',
    ],
    closer: 'Why do we still do it this way?',
  },
  {
    n: '02',
    title: 'Remove the unnecessary.',
    lines: [
      'The best solution doesn’t always require a new product.',
      'Sometimes it’s a better movement. A simpler mechanism. A different arrangement.',
      'Sometimes it’s something we can stop doing altogether.',
      'We believe an object should remove more friction than it creates.',
      'Fewer actions. Fewer objects. Fewer decisions.',
    ],
    closer: 'Not less functionality. Less complication.',
  },
  {
    n: '03',
    title: 'Make what remains exceptional.',
    lines: [
      'Simplicity shouldn’t come at the expense of quality.',
      'When something deserves a place in our lives, it should be a pleasure to use and worth keeping.',
      'Thoughtful proportions. Honest materials. Natural interactions. Lasting construction.',
      'Beauty and function aren’t competing ambitions.',
    ],
    closer: 'They’re parts of the same whole.',
  },
];

const approach = [
  ['Discover.', 'Find remarkable objects that quietly improve everyday life.'],
  ['Refine.', 'Remove what’s unnecessary. Improve what matters.'],
  ['Invent.', 'Create something new when existing solutions aren’t good enough.'],
];
---

<Base
  title="Our belief. Good design should remove more than it adds. Nomoro"
  description="The conviction behind Nomoro: good design should remove more than it adds. Three things we believe in, our approach, and why every object must earn its place."
>
  <!-- 01 Opening -->
  <section class="wrap pt-12 pb-24 lg:pt-24 lg:pb-40">
    <p class="eyebrow">Our belief</p>
    <h1 class="display mt-8 lg:mt-10 lg:max-w-[1171px]">Good design should remove more than it adds.</h1>

    <div class="mt-16 grid grid-cols-1 lg:mt-24 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-6">
      <div class="lg:col-start-5 lg:col-span-8 flex flex-col gap-10">
        <div>
          <p class="h2">We have more products than ever.</p>
          <p class="h2 text-steel">More tools. More features. More solutions.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-3 body-l">
          <p>Yet every new object asks something of us.</p>
          <p>A place to store it. Time to clean it. Another thing to maintain, repair, or eventually replace.</p>
          <p>We keep adding solutions without questioning the problems.</p>
        </div>
        <p class="h3">We believe good design should do the opposite.</p>
        <dl>
          {
            [
              ['Not add complexity.', 'Remove it.'],
              ['Not create unnecessary habits.', 'Improve the ones we already have.'],
              ['Not demand more attention.', 'Give some of it back.'],
            ].map(([a, b]) => (
              <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-1 border-t border-stone py-5 sm:grid-cols-2 sm:gap-6">
                <dt class="h3 text-steel">{a}</dt>
                <dd class="h3">{b}</dd>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </dl>
        <hr class="rule -mt-10" />
        <p class="h1">Less to do. More to life.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 02 Three things we believe in -->
  <section class="wrap pb-24 lg:pb-40" aria-labelledby="three-heading">
    <h2 id="three-heading" class="h2 mb-12">Three things we believe in.</h2>
    {
      beliefs.map((b) => (
        <article class="border-t border-ink grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 py-12 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-6 lg:py-16">
          <p class="display text-stone lg:col-span-2" aria-hidden="true">
            {b.n}
          </p>
          <h3 class="h2 lg:col-span-4">
            <span class="sr-only">{b.n}. </span>
            {b.title}
          </h3>
          <div class="lg:col-span-6 flex flex-col gap-4 body-l">
            {b.lines.map((l) => (
              <p>{l}</p>
            ))}
            <p class="standfirst pt-4">{b.closer}</p>
          </div>
        </article>
      ))
    }
    <hr class="rule-ink" />
  </section>

  <!-- 03 Approach -->
  <section class="wrap pb-24 lg:pb-40" aria-labelledby="approach-heading">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-6">
      <h2 id="approach-heading" class="h2 lg:col-span-7">
        We don’t believe every good idea needs to be invented again.
      </h2>
      <div class="lg:col-span-5 flex flex-col gap-3 body-l">
        <p>Some exceptional objects already exist. They simply deserve to be discovered.</p>
        <p>Others have the right idea but could be better.</p>
        <p>And sometimes, the right solution doesn’t exist yet.</p>
        <p>That’s why our approach is simple.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <dl class="mt-16 lg:mt-24">
      {
        approach.map(([w, d]) => (
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-3 border-t border-stone py-6 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-6 lg:items-start">
            <dt class="display lg:col-span-8">{w}</dt>
            <dd class="body-l lg:col-span-4 lg:pt-3">{d}</dd>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </dl>
    <hr class="rule" />
    <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-6">
      <div class="lg:col-start-9 lg:col-span-4">
        <p class="h3 text-steel">Different approaches. One ambition.</p>
        <p class="h3">Making everyday life a little better.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 04 Every object must earn its place. The one inverted section. -->
  <section class="inverted" aria-labelledby="earn-heading">
    <div class="wrap section flex flex-col gap-16 lg:gap-20">
      <h2 id="earn-heading" class="h1 lg:max-w-[1063px]">Every object must earn its place.</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-12 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-6">
        <div class="lg:col-span-6 flex flex-col gap-4">
          <p class="body-l">We don’t select things because they’re new, fashionable, or beautifully designed.</p>
          <ul class="mt-4" role="list">
            {
              [
                'We ask what they make better.',
                'What they make unnecessary.',
                'And whether someone will still be glad to own them years from now.',
              ].map((q) => (
                <li class="h3 border-t border-steel/60 py-4">{q}</li>
              ))
            }
          </ul>
          <hr class="rule -mt-4" />
        </div>
        <div class="lg:col-span-6 flex flex-col gap-4">
          <p class="body-l text-steel">
            Our selection principles are deliberately demanding. Not everything we admire belongs in the Nomoro
            collection.
          </p>
          <p class="body-l">And sometimes, the best recommendation is something we don’t sell.</p>
          <a href="/standard/" class="link body mt-4">Explore the Nomoro Standard →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 05 Close -->
  <section class="wrap pt-24 pb-16 lg:pt-40 lg:pb-24">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-6">
      <div class="lg:col-start-3 lg:col-span-7 flex flex-col gap-6">
        <h2 class="h2">A different kind of product company.</h2>
        <p class="body-l">
          Nomoro is beginning as an independent editorial project. A place to observe everyday life, investigate
          overlooked frustrations, and celebrate better solutions.
        </p>
        <p class="body-l">
          Over time, some discoveries may become part of a carefully selected collection. Others may inspire us
          to improve or create something new.
        </p>
        <div class="pt-2">
          <p class="h3 text-steel">But the collection isn’t the purpose.</p>
          <p class="h3">A better everyday life is.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="wrap pb-24 lg:pb-40 flex flex-col items-center gap-6">
    <div class="h-8 lg:h-10" style="color: var(--ink)"><Wordmark /></div>
    <p class="body-l">Less to do. More to life.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
